From: tomtomnet <tompere8000@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:21:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: add vdagent-clipboard-bridge for Wayland guests

spice-vdagent only knows the X11 clipboard.  GNOME keeps it in sync
with the Wayland one, but KDE Plasma only passes X11 copies on to
Wayland, and Hyprland and niri (xwayland-satellite) pass on neither, at
least for a client without a window like spice-vdagent.  The bridge
copies text between the two clipboards, in both directions, when they
differ, with wl-clipboard (the data-control protocol) and xclip.

Also document clipboard sharing in the README.

Local patch, not for upstream submission: QEMU does not accept
AI-generated code (docs/devel/code-provenance.rst).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
